{"step_index":116,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:06:19Z","input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_tokens":91862,"output_tokens":2408,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: APIs are functioning as expected, returning valid JSON data. The next step involves creating thorough documentation. This documentation will encompass a project overview, capabilities, and detailed explanations of each threat engine, including spyware/infostealer detection, antivirus/malware heuristics, and LOLRMM tracking of remote desktop control applications.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# 🛡️ AegisShield EDR - Cyber Process Monitor & Threat Eradicator\n\n> **Advanced Real-Time Spyware, Antivirus, Remote Desktop Control, Process Monitor, and Trojan Detection Dashboard**\n> *Scans your system, identifies threats via multi-vector heuristics and threat intelligence, and kills them with a single click.*\n\n---\n\n## 🌟 Key Features\n\n### 1. 🕵️ Spyware & Infostealer Detection\n* **Keylogger & Hook Inspection:** Scans binary imports and memory hooks for keystroke logging (`SetWindowsHookEx`, `GetAsyncKeyState`, `GetKeyboardState`).\n* **Screen Scraping & Surveillance:** Detects hidden screen recording APIs (`BitBlt`, `GetDC`) and unauthorized background input capture.\n* **Infostealer Heuristics:** Matches signatures of notorious credential stealers like **AgentTesla**, **RedLine**, **Vidar**, and LSASS dumpers like **Mimikatz**.\n\n### 2. 🦠 Antivirus & Malware Engine\n* **Pure-Python PE Binary Header Analysis:** Extracts COFF headers, architecture, and section structures without requiring external C extensions.\n* **Shannon Entropy Analysis:** Identifies crypted, packed, or UPX-obfuscated executables (Entropy > 7.15).\n* **System Process Masquerading:** Flags processes pretending to be Windows system binaries (e.g. `svchost.exe`, `lsass.exe`, `csrss.exe`) running outside `C:\\Windows\\System32`.\n* **Typosquatting Detection:** Detects deceptive names like `svch0st.exe`, `lsasss.exe`, `scvhost.exe`, `taskmngr.exe`, and `dwm0.exe`.\n* **Suspicious Drop Zones:** Detects and flags executables executing out of `%TEMP%`, `Users\\Public`, `Downloads`, or the Recycle Bin.\n* **LOLBins & Obfuscation Heuristics:** Catches encoded PowerShell (`-enc`, `-encodedcommand`), hidden windows (`-w hidden`), download cradles (`IEX Net.WebClient`), `certutil` downloaders, and ransomware volume shadow deletion (`vssadmin delete shadows`).\n\n### 3. 📡 Remote Desktop & RMM Detector (LOLRMM)\n* **Living Off The Land RMM Tracking:** Automatically discovers 60+ dual-use commercial & open-source remote access tools:\n  * **AnyDesk** (Port 7070, 6568)\n  * **TeamViewer** (Port 5938)\n  * **RustDesk** (Ports 21115 - 21119)\n  * **ConnectWise ScreenConnect** (Ports 8040, 8041)\n  * **VNC Servers** (UltraVNC, RealVNC, TightVNC on ports 5900 - 5905)\n  * **Splashtop**, **LogMeIn**, **Atera**, **NinjaRMM**, **NetSupport Manager**, **Ammyy Admin**, and **Remote Utilities**.\n* **Reverse Tunnels & C2 Proxies:** Detects persistent reverse tunnels often abused by attackers (**Ngrok**, **Cloudflared**, **FRP**, **Chisel**, **Ligolo**).\n* **Network Sockets Correlation:** Maps listening and active established remote control sockets directly to PIDs.\n\n### 4. 🐴 Trojan & RAT Eradication\n* **Known RAT Signatures:** Real-time identification of **njRAT (Bladabindi)**, **AsyncRAT**, **QuasarRAT**, **Remcos RAT**, **DarkComet**, **NanoCore**, **Cobalt Strike Beacons**, **Sliver**, and **XMRig Cryptominers**.\n* **Suspicious Parent-Child Trees:** Detects Office documents (`WINWORD.EXE`, `EXCEL.EXE`) or PDF readers spawning command interpreters (`cmd.exe`, `powershell.exe`).\n\n### 5. ⚡ Process Eradication & Remediation (\"Finds it and Kills it\")\n* **Instant Process Termination:** Forcefully terminates rogue processes (`proc.kill()`).\n* **Recursive Tree Eradication:** Kills parent processes and all spawned child processes to prevent surviving beacons.\n* **🚨 Emergency Bulk Kill:** Single-click eradication for all detected threats matching or exceeding threat thresholds.\n* **Core OS Protection Whitelist:** Automatically protects critical Windows OS components (`smss.exe`, `csrss.exe`, `lsass.exe`, `services.exe` in `C:\\Windows\\System32`) from accidental termination.\n* **Threat Quarantine:** Isolates suspicious binaries into `quarantine/` with execution rights revoked and forensic receipts.\n* **Persistence Neutralization:** Scans and disables malicious autorun items in Windows Startup folders, Registry Run keys (`HKCU`/`HKLM`), and Scheduled Tasks.\n\n### 6. 🧪 Built-in Safe Threat Simulation Lab\n* Verify detection and remediation safely without real malware!\n* Launch simulated benign test processes exhibiting Temp execution, encoded cradles, or RMM beaconing.\n* Watch AegisShield flag them with high risk scores and terminate them with one click.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start Guide\n\n### Option 1: Double-Click Launcher (Windows)\nSimply double-click the included batch launcher:\n```bat\nstart_dashboard.bat\n```\nThis automatically starts the backend server and launches the Web Dashboard at `http://127.0.0.1:8888`.\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Python Command Line\n\n#### 1. Start Web Dashboard\n```bash\npython run_server.py\n```\nOpen your browser to: **`http://localhost:8888`**\n\n#### 2. Terminal CLI Scanner\nYou can also scan and kill threats directly from PowerShell / CMD:\n```bash\n# Run deep system threat scan\npython cli_scanner.py --scan\n\n# Scan and automatically kill all detected threats\npython cli_scanner.py --scan --kill\n\n# Check specifically for Remote Desktop / RMM / VNC tools\npython cli_scanner.py --rmm\n\n# Audit startup and registry persistence\npython cli_scanner.py --persistence\n\n# Terminate single process by PID\npython cli_scanner.py --kill-pid 1234\n\n# Eradicate process and all children\npython cli_scanner.py --kill-tree 1234\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📁 Project Architecture\n\n```\nSpywareProcessMon/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── config.py              # Configuration, whitelists, critical binaries, ports\n│   ├── signatures_db.py       # Catalog of LOLRMM tools, RATs, infostealers, heuristics\n│   ├── pe_analyzer.py         # Pure-Python PE parser, Shannon entropy, API string scanner\n│   ├── network_monitor.py     # Sockets, listening ports, remote connections, RMM ports\n│   ├── persistence_hunter.py  # Startup folders, Registry Run keys, Scheduled Tasks\n│   ├── detector.py            # Multi-vector detection engine (7 analysis passes)\n│   ├── remediator.py          # Kill engine, process tree terminator, quarantine, audit log\n│   ├── simulator.py           # Benign threat simulator for safe verification\n│   └── server.py              # FastAPI REST API + WebSockets telemetry server\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── index.html             # Cyber SOC Dashboard UI\n│   ├── css/\n│   │   └── dashboard.css      # Dark SOC cyber styling, animations, glow effects\n│   └── js/\n│       └── app.js             # Real-time WebSocket/polling, state management, audio chimes\n├── cli_scanner.py             # CLI tool for terminal scans and kills\n├── run_server.py              # Server launcher script with automatic browser open\n├── start_dashboard.bat        # Windows 1-click batch launcher\n├── requirements.txt           # Python dependencies (fastapi, uvicorn, psutil, requests)\n└── README.md                  # Complete documentation\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Detection Logic & Scoring Matrix\n\nAegisShield evaluates running processes across 7 distinct detection vectors to compute a **Threat Score (0 to 100)**:\n\n| Risk Level | Score Range | Primary Action | UI Indicator |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **CRITICAL** | 80 – 100 | Immediate Eradication Recommended | Pulsing Crimson Border |\n| **HIGH** | 60 – 79 | Dangerous Anomaly / Unauthorized RMM | Amber Warning |\n| **MEDIUM** | 40 – 59 | Suspicious Behavior / Drop Zone | Violet Alert |\n| **LOW** | 20 – 39 | Minor Anomaly / Review | Slate Informational |\n| **SAFE** | 0 – 19 | Legitimate Process | Emerald Green |\n\n---\n\n## 🔒 Security & Safety Controls\n1. **Critical System Whitelist:** Protected system processes (`system`, `registry`, `smss.exe`, `csrss.exe`, `wininit.exe`, `services.exe`, `lsass.exe`) running from verified `System32` paths cannot be terminated, preventing blue screens (BSOD).\n2. **Audit Trail:** Every scan, process termination, tree kill, or quarantine action is logged with exact timestamps in `logs/audit_events.json` and exportable directly as JSON.\n3. **Safe Simulation:** The built-in simulation scenarios only sleep and exit safely, ensuring 100% safety for training and verification.\n\n---\n\n## 📄 License\nMIT License. Built for endpoint defense, threat hunting, and educational cybersecurity research.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"c:\\Users\\thann\\Downloads\\AntiGravity\\SpywareProcessMon\\README.md"}}]}
