{"step_index":120,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:06:49Z","input_tokens":3331,"cache_read_tokens":95122,"output_tokens":2702,"content":"# 🛡️ AegisShield EDR - Cyber Threat Hunter, Process Monitor & Eradicator\n\nI have designed and built **AegisShield EDR**, a real-time **Spyware, Antivirus, Remote Desktop Control (LOLRMM), Process Monitor, and Trojan Detection & Eradication Platform** with a modern SOC (Security Operations Center) Web Dashboard and CLI utility.\n\n---\n\n### 🌐 Key Capabilities Built\n\n1. **🕵️ Spyware & Infostealer Detection:**\n   - **Keylogger & Hook Inspection:** Scans binary imports and API references for keystroke monitoring ([`SetWindowsHookEx`](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/signatures_db.py#L231), [`GetAsyncKeyState`](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/signatures_db.py#L234), `GetKeyboardState`).\n   - **Screen Surveillance:** Detects hidden screen recording APIs (`BitBlt`, `GetDC`) and unauthorized background input capture.\n   - **Credential Stealers:** Signatures for notorious infostealers like **AgentTesla**, **RedLine**, **Vidar**, and LSASS dumpers like **Mimikatz**.\n\n2. **🦠 Antivirus & Malware Engine:**\n   - **Pure-Python PE Header Inspection:** Extracts COFF headers, architecture, and section structures without requiring external C extensions.\n   - **Shannon Entropy Analysis:** Identifies packed, crypted, or UPX-obfuscated executables (Entropy > 7.15).\n   - **System Process Masquerading:** Flags processes masquerading as Windows system binaries (e.g. `svchost.exe`, `lsass.exe`, `csrss.exe`) running outside `C:\\Windows\\System32`.\n   - **Typosquatting Detection:** Detects deceptive names like `svch0st.exe`, `lsasss.exe`, `scvhost.exe`, `taskmngr.exe`, and `dwm0.exe`.\n   - **Suspicious Drop Zones:** Identifies executables executing out of `%TEMP%`, `Users\\Public`, `Downloads`, or the Recycle Bin.\n   - **LOLBins Heuristics:** Catches encoded PowerShell (`-enc`, `-encodedcommand`), hidden windows (`-w hidden`), download cradles (`IEX Net.WebClient`), `certutil` downloaders, and ransomware volume shadow deletion (`vssadmin delete shadows`).\n\n3. **📡 Remote Desktop & RMM Detector (LOLRMM):**\n   - **Living Off The Land RMM Tracking:** Automatically discovers 60+ dual-use commercial & open-source remote access tools:\n     - **AnyDesk** (Port 7070, 6568)\n     - **TeamViewer** (Port 5938)\n     - **RustDesk** (Ports 21115 - 21119)\n     - **ConnectWise ScreenConnect** (Ports 8040, 8041)\n     - **VNC Servers** (UltraVNC, RealVNC, TightVNC on ports 5900 - 5905)\n     - **Splashtop**, **LogMeIn**, **Atera**, **NinjaRMM**, **NetSupport Manager**, **Ammyy Admin**, and **Remote Utilities**.\n   - **Reverse Tunnels & C2 Proxies:** Detects persistent reverse tunnels often abused by attackers (**Ngrok**, **Cloudflared**, **FRP**, **Chisel**, **Ligolo**).\n   - **Network Sockets Correlation:** Maps listening and active established remote control sockets directly to PIDs.\n\n4. **🐴 Trojan & RAT Eradication:**\n   - **Known RAT Signatures:** Real-time identification of **njRAT (Bladabindi)**, **AsyncRAT**, **QuasarRAT**, **Remcos RAT**, **DarkComet**, **NanoCore**, **Cobalt Strike Beacons**, **Sliver**, and **XMRig Cryptominers**.\n   - **Suspicious Parent-Child Trees:** Detects Office documents (`WINWORD.EXE`, `EXCEL.EXE`) or PDF readers spawning command interpreters (`cmd.exe`, `powershell.exe`).\n\n5. **⚡ Threat Eradication (\"Finds it and Kills it\"):**\n   - **Instant Process Termination:** Forcefully terminates rogue processes (`proc.kill()`).\n   - **Recursive Tree Eradication:** Kills parent processes and all spawned child processes to prevent surviving beacons.\n   - **🚨 Emergency Bulk Kill:** Single-click eradication for all detected threats matching or exceeding threat thresholds.\n   - **Core OS Protection Whitelist:** Automatically protects critical Windows OS components (`smss.exe`, `csrss.exe`, `lsass.exe`, `services.exe` in `C:\\Windows\\System32`) from accidental termination.\n   - **Threat Quarantine:** Isolates suspicious binaries into `quarantine/` with execution rights revoked and forensic receipts.\n   - **Persistence Neutralization:** Scans and disables malicious autorun items in Windows Startup folders, Registry Run keys (`HKCU`/`HKLM`), and Scheduled Tasks.\n\n6. **🧪 Safe Threat Simulation Lab:**\n   - Built directly into the dashboard to safely test and demonstrate detection and kill capabilities without risking actual malware on your PC.\n\n---\n\n### 📂 File Structure\n\n* [**`start_dashboard.bat`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/start_dashboard.bat): 1-click Windows batch file to launch the server and open the browser.\n* [**`run_server.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/run_server.py): Server launcher script that starts the backend and automatically opens `http://127.0.0.1:8888`.\n* [**`cli_scanner.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/cli_scanner.py): Full CLI terminal scanner with color-coded alerts and process killing controls.\n* [**`frontend/index.html`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/frontend/index.html): Dark Cyber SOC UI with real-time gauges, live telemetry, and eradication controls.\n* [**`frontend/css/dashboard.css`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/frontend/css/dashboard.css): Styling, pulse effects, and glassmorphism.\n* [**`frontend/js/app.js`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/frontend/js/app.js): WebSocket telemetry, kill actions, Web Audio alert synthesizer.\n* [**`backend/detector.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/detector.py): Multi-vector detection engine.\n* [**`backend/remediator.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/remediator.py): Process killer, tree terminator, quarantine, and audit log.\n* [**`backend/signatures_db.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/signatures_db.py): LOLRMM database, RAT IOCs, and command line heuristics.\n* [**`backend/network_monitor.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/network_monitor.py): TCP/UDP socket tracker and RMM port detector.\n* [**`backend/persistence_hunter.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/persistence_hunter.py): Startup, Registry Run keys, and Scheduled Tasks inspector.\n* [**`backend/pe_analyzer.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/pe_analyzer.py): Pure-Python PE parser, Shannon entropy, and API scanner.\n* [**`backend/simulator.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/simulator.py): Benign threat simulation test suite.\n* [**`README.md`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/README.md): Detailed documentation and user manual.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 How to Run\n\n#### Option 1: Double-Click Launcher\nDouble-click [**`start_dashboard.bat`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/start_dashboard.bat) in the project directory. It starts the server and opens your browser directly to:\n👉 **`http://127.0.0.1:8888`**\n\n#### Option 2: Python Command\nRun in your terminal:\n```bash\npython run_server.py\n```\n\n#### Option 3: Command-Line Scanner (CLI)\nYou can also run scans and kill threats directly from PowerShell / CMD:\n```bash\n# 1. Deep system threat scan\npython cli_scanner.py --scan\n\n# 2. Deep scan and automatically kill all detected threats\npython cli_scanner.py --scan --kill\n\n# 3. Check for active Remote Desktop / RMM / VNC connections\npython cli_scanner.py --rmm\n\n# 4. Check Windows Startup and Registry persistence\npython cli_scanner.py --persistence\n\n# 5. Kill a specific process by PID\npython cli_scanner.py --kill-pid <PID>\n\n# 6. Kill process and all child processes recursively\npython cli_scanner.py --kill-tree <PID>\n```","thinking":"Reviewing the user requirements, the objective involves several distinct components: spyware and infostealer detection (targeting keylogging, screenshots, and specific malware families), an antivirus/malware engine (focused on PE header analysis, entropy thresholds, and common masquerading techniques), and remote access detection.\n\n\n"}
